# oracle: cut-down examples/body/in.pour3d: one rounded rod molecule (molecule.rod3d, 2 vertices, 1 edge, rounded diameter 0.5; the nsub 2 branch) poured with fix pour mol (seed 4767548, vol 0.4 10) into a slab above a fix wall/body/polyhedron floor, pair body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5 with pair_coeff * * 100 1, fix nve/body, fix gravity, 3000 steps: thermo atoms ke pe etotal press and the atom state
# Measured max relative error: 2.0e-11 (fy of atom 1; thermo exact zeros; positions 4.9e-14, velocities 2.2e-12). Native: installed lmp (LAMMPS 2 Sep 2026, BODY package). The rod inertia is degenerate (Ixx = Iyy), so the body frame relies on the native selection-sort order of the axes (bodies.ts nativeFrame); the fixture has 2 rods by step 500 and 4 by step 2500.
# oracle-inputs: w152body_pour_rod.mol
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
boundary        p p fm
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 8
region          reg block 0 20 0 20 0 20 units box
create_box      1 reg
molecule        obj w152body_pour_rod.mol
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
fix             2 all gravity 1.0 spherical 0.0 -180.0
region          slab block 5 15 5 15 3 6 units box
fix             ins all pour 8 0 4767548 vol 0.4 10 region slab mol obj
fix             4 all wall/body/polyhedron 2000 50 50 zplane 0.0 NULL
thermo_style    custom step atoms ke pe etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          500
run             3000
